# L §3.1 A day key where a date is expected (2.1-C7b-19): "A day index is days or a range of day periods without by n,
# or by 1 (§4.1). A key of a month or a year index, or of a day range by n with n above 1, doesn't convert".  A key of
# a day range by 1 is a day: min(w, cutoff) means min(start_of(w), cutoff), here the key's own day 2026-01-05 (carried
# through).  (L3_1_day_key_by_n keeps by 7 refused.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input cutoff: date
index dd = day 2026-01-05..2026-12-28 by 1
def lo[w in dd]: date = min(w, cutoff) at cutoff
ask q: lo[2026-01-05]

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  cutoff = 2026-03-10
=== expect
q: 2026-01-05
...
